  "question": {
    "text": "Block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>of mass m and block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></math> are placed on a fixed triangular wedge by means of a massless, inextensible string and a frictionless pulley as shown in the figure. The wedge is inclined at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>°</mo></math> to the horizontal on both sides. The coefficient of friction between block A and the wedge is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and that between block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and the wedge is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. If the blocks <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> are released from rest, find the acceleration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0009112_Ques1_1..jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"height: 151px; width: 230px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
