  "solution": {
    "text": "Acceleration of block A:<br />Maximum friction force that can be obtained at A is<br />&nbsp;<br />(f<sub>max</sub>)<sub>A</sub> =μ<sub>A</sub>(mg cos 45<sup>0</sup>) = <math><mrow><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></math>(mg /√2) = <math><mrow><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></math><br />&nbsp;<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0009112_AnsExp1_1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 366px; height: 222px;\" /><br /><br />Similarly,<br /><br />(f<sub>max</sub> )<sub>B</sub> = μ<sub>B</sub> (2mg cos 45°) = <math><mrow><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo maxsize=\"1.00em\">(</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize=\"1.00em\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></math><br /><br />Therefore, maximum value of friction that can be obtained on the system is <math><mrow><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></math><br /><br />Net pulling force on the system is<br />&nbsp;<br />F = F<sub>1</sub>-F<sub>2</sub> =<math><mrow><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>.... (ii)<br />&nbsp;<br />From Eqs. (i) and (ii), we can see that Net pulling force &lt; f<sub>max</sub><br />&nbsp;<br />Therefore, the system will not move or the acceleration of block A will be zero.",
